          "amounts": {
            "subtotal": 100,
            "tax": 0,
            "total": 100
          },
          "currency": "USD"
        }
      },
      "outputShape": "body.valid (bool), body.errors[] ({field,issue} required-field failures), body.warnings[] ({field,issue} recommended/EU-compliance gaps), body.tax_calculation_check {expected_tax,actual_tax,difference,pass}, body.line_items_check {total_checked,passed,failed}, body.eu_compliant (bool)",
      "quirks": [
        "inputSchema is null in the registry; wrap the invoice under an 'invoice' key. The validator's canonical required fields are: invoice_date, vendor_name, vendor_vat, vendor_address, amounts (object with subtotal/tax/total). Recommended (warning-only) fields: buyer_name, buyer_vat, buyer_address, due_date. Each line item should include line_total or it cannot verify line math.",
        "Sending unknown/extra field names does NOT error the call (HTTP 200 always for a well-formed JSON body); the validator simply reports missing required fields as errors. So a wrong field name yields valid:false rather than a 4xx.",
        "body.valid:false is a normal successful response indicating the invoice has issues, not an endpoint failure."
      ],
      "needs": [],
      "needsApproval": false,
      "guide": "POST a JSON body to https://api.strale.io/x402/invoice-validate with an \"invoice\" object containing the invoice fields. The canonical fields the validator checks are invoice_date, vendor_name, vendor_vat, vendor_address, an amounts object {subtotal,tax,total}, and line_items[] each with a line_total. Pay $0.0216 USDC on Base via x402 (no API key, no sign-in). Read body.valid for the pass/fail verdict, body.errors[] for blocking required-field problems, body.warnings[] for EU-compliance recommendations, and tax_calculation_check / line_items_check for math validation. A valid:false response is still a successful call.",
